    "resident": "Hethra, who went down after the note when the doors fell and has held it since, and the choristers who came to sing it with her",
    "story": "A long way in and down under the Choir plateau, cut by the Builders through rock that the Ash Winter turned partly to glass: galleries where the note runs along the walls like water, a rift, a shaft up to the plateau's light, a black lake that does not move when the note does, the knights' hall where the Order's last knight still stands his watch, and at the bottom the hall where the note was struck, with something in the middle of it holding it.",
    "unique_object": "a tuning-stone in the hall of the struck note, a column of the Builders' black stone that hums under the hand, worn smooth to the height of a mouth",
