    "story": "The runs under the casting floor of the Builders' foundry: the fire-mouth going down, the gallery where the metal ran in channels cut in the rock, the pouring floor with its crucibles, the loam store where the founders slept, a shaft fallen in, the rift the metal once spilled into, the pattern-hall where the shapes of every bell the city cast are kept, and the pit under the last bell, where the Bellwright stands with his hand on its lip.",
    "unique_object": "a channel cut in the gallery floor still lined with a skin of bronze, running down towards the pit, warm",
